`a()` calls `b()`, which calls `c()`, which throws an `Error`. Put the function frames in the order they appear in `err.stack`, from the first line after the message to the last.

```js
function a() { b(); }
function b() { c(); }
function c() { throw new Error('boom'); }
try { a(); } catch (err) { console.log(err.stack); }
```

