```

A third-party SDK exposes `charge(card, callback)`. After a network retry, it sometimes calls `callback(null, receipt)` twice, and your code ships the order twice. Wrapping it like this fixes the duplicate shipments:

```js
const chargeAsync = (card) =>
  new Promise((resolve, reject) =>
    charge(card, (err, receipt) => (err ? reject(err) : resolve(receipt))));

const receipt = await chargeAsync(card);
shipOrder(receipt);
```

Why?
